From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:07:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PVE backup: vma reader: fix blob buffer bounds check wrapping
 around

The bounds check for the blob buffer adds its offset and size, both
32-bit values taken from the archive header. A crafted header can make
that sum wrap around, for example with an offset just below 4 GiB and a
small size, so the check passes and parsing the blob buffer reads far
outside of the header data. That crashes vma already with 'vma list'.

Check the offset and the size against the header size separately, so
no sum can wrap around. Archives created by vma always place the blob
buffer directly after the fixed header part, which passes the stricter
checks.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 vma-reader.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vma-reader.c b/vma-reader.c
index ebd17c907c..ab0fe6f3b7 100644
--- a/vma-reader.c
+++ b/vma-reader.c
@@ -286,13 +286,15 @@ static int vma_reader_read_head(VmaReader *vmar, Error **errp)
     uint32_t bstart = h->blob_buffer_offset + 1;
     uint32_t bend = h->blob_buffer_offset + h->blob_buffer_size;
 
-    if (bstart <= sizeof(VmaHeader)) {
+    if (h->blob_buffer_offset < sizeof(VmaHeader) ||
+        h->blob_buffer_offset >= header_size) {
         error_setg(errp, "wrong vma blob buffer offset %d",
                    h->blob_buffer_offset);
         return -1;
     }
 
-    if (bend > header_size) {
+    /* compare with the remaining size, the end offset could wrap around */
+    if (h->blob_buffer_size > header_size - h->blob_buffer_offset) {
         error_setg(errp, "wrong vma blob buffer size %d/%d",
                    h->blob_buffer_offset, h->blob_buffer_size);
         return -1;
